@startuml
title Interceptor / AOP Interceptor / Filter

skinparam legendBackgroundColor #f9f9f9
skinparam legendBorderColor #999999

legend right

**Intent**:
Provide hotspots to add cross-cutting concerns dynamically (logging, auth, metrics).

**Motivation**:
Insert behavior before/after method invocation without modifying core code.

**Applicability**:
Aspect-oriented needs; pluggable pipelines; request processing.

**Participants**:
InterceptorChain executes interceptors around a Target.

**Consequences**:
Pros: Modular cross-cutting concerns; easy enabling/disabling.
Cons: Ordering dependencies; debugging stacks.

**Implementation Notes**:
Define well-formed proceed() semantics; handle exceptions uniformly.
Combine with annotations/metadata for selection.

**Known Uses**:
Java EE Interceptors; Spring AOP; Servlet Filters; gRPC interceptors.

**Related Patterns**:
Decorator, Chain of Responsibility, Proxy.

endlegend

class InvocationContext {
  +proceed()
  +getData()
}

interface Interceptor {
  +intercept(ctx: InvocationContext)
}

class LoggingInterceptor
class AuthInterceptor

class InterceptorChain {
  -interceptors : List<Interceptor>
  +add(i: Interceptor)
  +invoke(ctx: InvocationContext)
}

class Target {
  +handle(ctx: InvocationContext)
}

Interceptor <|.. LoggingInterceptor
Interceptor <|.. AuthInterceptor
InterceptorChain o-- Interceptor
InterceptorChain ..> Target : delegates via ctx.proceed()
@enduml